Reports to the Payroll & Benefits Manager and works closely with the HR Managers and head of Finance. Processes bi-weekly payroll for certain entities for office/plant employees and is the first point of contact for employees in matter of time, attendance, benefits and payroll. Duties and responsibilities include but are not limited to:
Education
Bachelor's Degree or diploma in Accounting, Finance, or Human Resources Management is preferred;
Payroll Compliance Practitioner Certification is an asset.
Years of Experience
Minimum 3+ years of payroll experience.
Working Conditions
Hours of operation: 8:30 AM - 5:00 PM Monday to Friday;
Flexible to work overtime, must get approval before; and
Requires wearing PPE in certain locations.
Required Level
Experience with Ceridian Dayforce HCM software;
Proficient in Microsoft Office, Outlook and Excel;
Demonstrates State's core values;
Strong attention to detail and accuracy is required;
Proficient in data entry management;
Exercise critical thinking methods to identify and solve problems;
Knowledgeable about labour/payroll legislations and ensure the Company is compliant;
Demonstrates positivity and dependability; and
Processes payroll and maintain employee confidentiality without supervision.
Job Specific Duties
Time Clock and Ceridian Management: Set up users in the timeclock as required and provide employees with Dayforce logins and or password changes;
Adding New Hires, Salary Adjustments/Garnishments/Benefits or Removing Employees: Work closely with the HR Managers to receive payroll information, set up new hires, terminate users, resignations, leaves, vacation pay and pay increases;
