Process year end T4's;
Completion of applicable T4A's and submission to Revenue Canada;
Responsible for monthly collection of mileage logs;
Reporting: Labour, O/T, employee headcounts, salaries, bonuses, Monthly Company hours for WSIB purposes, turnover, new hires, attendance, vacation, WSIB remittances, and payroll summaries;
Benefits and Administration: Print, track, reconcile invoices and employee expenses (Beneplan, TB prescription eyeglasses, MSS);
Responsible for enrolling and removing employees on the benefits;
Update addresses on employee benefits;
Administrate Mister Safety Shoes Program;
Processing and Approvals: Responsible for submitting weekly agency timesheets, reconciling invoices and discrepancies;
Ceridian Invoices as required;
Inform the Payroll & Benefits Manager and HR Managers before making any decisions that will affect staff, payroll and or legal;
Other: Investigate and answer employee questions associated with their pay and benefits;
Responsible for filing and maintaining employee documents;
Track intercompany transactions as required;
Responsible for employment letters;
Upkeep the State payroll training manual as required;
Calculation of Company Allocation adjustment including the Employer portion of CPP/EI/EHT amount;
Answer Service Canada inquiries as required; and
Any other tasks assigned by the Payroll & Benefit Manager/HR Manager/CFO.
